Changes: strict CP949 decoding; active-status records only; bare native single-lot address extraction; EPSG:5174 to longitude/latitude EPSG:4326 conversion with PROJ; duplicate removal; whole-source shared-point and raw coordinate-spread quarantine. The builder admits only geometry-corroborated lots whose folded name/number pair was absent from its earlier Korean inputs. No benchmark or held-out answers select source rows.

These are registered business parcel/address reference points, not verified entrances or complete residential coverage. Lot-derived houses are excluded from house reverse-geocoding postings. Multi-parcel, floor/unit annotations and ambiguous or unsupported source records are not admitted by this supplement. Existing house coordinates and postcodes take precedence.
